From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:33:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] feat: diagnostic-only /debug/simulate_restart endpoint
 (NOW.md ladder level 3)

Drops the RAM prompt cache and rebuilds it from the disk tier in-process,
without killing and relaunching the server -- skips the ~15-20s model
reload so a "post-restart cold turn" microbenchmark costs one HTTP
request instead of a real process restart. The only externally-visible
difference from a real restart this doesn't reproduce is that reload
time; the cache state afterward is the same starting point.

Refactored _generate()'s inline load-on-start block into
ResponseGenerator._restore_from_disk(), now shared by real startup and
this endpoint's restart path (_simulate_restart_now()). The restart runs
on the generation thread, not the HTTP handler thread: it shares
LRUPromptCache state with every real request without a lock (the
generation thread is meant to be its sole owner) and MLX needs a stream
bound to whichever thread evaluates the reloaded arrays -- the same class
of bug already fixed twice for other threads in this cache (0009, and the
flush-on-shutdown fix in an earlier round). request_simulated_restart()
queues the work and blocks on an Event until the generation thread's main
loop drains it, rather than calling the cache directly from the HTTP
thread.

Diagnostic-only per NOW.md: never gate evidence on its own, only for
screening ladder levers and restore-path work at the "cold-turn
microbench on a store fixture" iteration-speed level.
